  ($q$alg-84$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in one variable$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the largest integer value of x that satisfies −3x + 4 ≥ −11?$q$, $q$["5","−5","4","6"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$−3x + 4 ≥ −11 → −3x ≥ −15 → x ≤ 5 (the inequality flips when dividing by a negative number), so the largest integer value is 5.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-85$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in one variable$q$, 1, null, $q$A vending machine snack costs $1.50. If Jordan has $12 and wants to keep at least $3 remaining, what is the maximum number of snacks Jordan can buy?$q$, $q$["6","8","9","5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$1.50n ≤ 12 − 3 = 9 → n ≤ 6, so the maximum number of snacks is 6.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-86$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in one variable$q$, 2, null, $q$What is the greatest integer value of x that satisfies −5 < 3x − 2 ≤ 10?$q$, $q$["4","3","−1","5"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$−5 < 3x − 2 ≤ 10 → −3 < 3x ≤ 12 → −1 < x ≤ 4, so the greatest integer value is 4.$q$, null),
