  ($q$alg-94$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Linear inequalities in two variables$q$, 2, null, $q$The point (1, −1) lies on the boundary line of 8x + 8y ≤ k. What is the value of k?$q$, $q$["−1","4","2","0"]$q$::jsonb, 3, $q$Since (1, −1) is on the boundary line 8x + 8y = k, substituting gives k = 8(1) + 8(−1) = 0.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-95$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Word problems$q$, 2, null, $q$A rectangular garden has a perimeter of 54 feet. The length is 3 feet more than twice the width. What is the width of the garden, in feet?$q$, $q$["8","19","9","7"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Perimeter: 2(l + w) = 54 → l + w = 27. Since l = 2w + 3: (2w + 3) + w = 27 → 3w = 24 → w = 8.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-96$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Word problems$q$, 2, null, $q$A theater sold 200 tickets for a play, some at $18 for adults and the rest at $10 for children, collecting $2,960 total. How many adult tickets were sold?$q$, $q$["120","80","100","150"]$q$::jsonb, 0, $q$Let a + c = 200 and 18a + 10c = 2960. Substituting c = 200 − a: 18a + 10(200 − a) = 2960 → 8a + 2000 = 2960 → a = 120.$q$, null),
  ($q$alg-97$q$, $q$math$q$, $q$Algebra$q$, $q$Word problems$q$, 2, null, $q$Working alone, machine A fills 3 boxes per hour, and machine B fills 2 boxes per hour. Working together at these rates, how many hours will it take them to fill 40 boxes?$q$, $q$["5","9","8","−8"]$q$::jsonb, 2, $q$Together the machines fill 3 + 2 = 5 boxes per hour. To fill 40 boxes takes 40/5 = 8 hours.$q$, null),
